(footprint "SCHURTER_SCPC_WS17"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "SCHURTER SCPC Case WS17 prismatic supercapacitor (P/N 3-153-438), 1.0 F 2.75 V, ESR 40 mOhm. Flat prismatic cell 28.5 x 17.0 mm, 1.70 mm max thick. Under-body solder pads only: N 12.25 x 3.5 and P 7.75 x 3.5, centred +/-12.30 mm from cell centre (outer edge 0.20 mm in from each body end) and laterally OPPOSED -- N sits 1.50 mm in from one long edge, P 1.50 mm in from the other, so the pair runs diagonally. Pad width AND that lateral offset are the polarity key. The end tabs (drawn on F.Fab, ~2.75 mm past each end) are finish-coated locators, NOT solder pads. CORRECTED 2026-08-03, measured off the Case WS10/WS13/WS17 bottom views: the datasheet's 1.5 +/-0.5 is a LATERAL inset from a long edge, not an end inset. Read as an end inset it put both pads on the centreline at +/-11.0 -- 1.30 mm per side too far in, and with P overhanging its 7.75 terminal by ~3.1 mm onto the bare can. The board's embedded land (Downloads:SCHURTER_SCPC_WS17-mod2) still carries the old geometry; correcting it needs a B-side re-route, see PCB/README.md.")
	(tags "supercapacitor SCHURTER SCPC WS17 3-153-438 prismatic")
